# Sandbox Limitations

The Cursor agent shell runs inside a **sandbox** that blocks outbound network access.

## Blocked operations (NEVER attempt these)

- `ssh` — any SSH commands, including deploy to VPS
- `scp`, `rsync` over SSH
- `git push`, `git pull`, `git fetch` — any remote git operations
- `docker` commands that pull/push images from registries
- `curl`, `wget`, `Invoke-WebRequest` to external hosts
- Any command that requires network connectivity to external servers

## What to do instead

- **Deploy to VPS**: Tell the user the exact commands to run manually in their own terminal. Format them as a ready-to-copy code block.
- **Git push/pull**: Same — provide the commands for the user to execute.
- **Docker pull**: Provide the command for the user.

## Key rule

Do NOT try a network command "just to check" — it will always fail in sandbox. Go straight to providing the user with commands to run manually.
